{
  "about": "Rolling bearings the selection (GBX-3) chooses from: boundary dimensions (ISO 15, ISO 355) and ratings as a maker's public catalogue lists them. Lengths in mm, ratings in kN. For tapered roller bearings, width is the total width T, and a is SKF's \"distance side face to pressure point\": measured along the axis from the large side face of the outer ring (its back face, the face the total width T is also measured from; SKF's dimension drawing) to the bearing's pressure centre, where SKF takes the radial load to act (SKF, single row tapered roller bearings, Loads: \"The radial loads act at the pressure centres of the bearings\", distance a in each product's technical specification). Where a exceeds T, as in the steep-angle 313 series, the pressure centre lies outside the bearing, beyond the inner ring's back face. Every row carries its source and whether it was checked against that source.",
  "source": "SKF, rolling bearings catalogue (public product data on skf.com)",
